2026-10-25T02:59:08.6698370Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6728500Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6730510Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6735870Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6737100Z 
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6737390Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6737810Z 
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6739160Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6741860Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6742540Z 
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6742750Z If you would like to
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6743030Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6743350Z 
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6743660Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-25T02:59:08.6744040Z   $ sh ./install-nix
